<section class="wm-hero"><svg class="wm-topo" viewBox="0 0 1440 900" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M624 450 C 660 396, 738 408, 792 450 S 756 498, 624 450" style="--k:0"/><path d="M512 450 C 590 333, 759 359, 876 450 S 798 554, 512 450" style="--k:1"/><path d="M400 450 C 520 270, 780 310, 960 450 S 840 610, 400 450" style="--k:2"/><path d="M288 450 C 450 207, 801 261, 1044 450 S 882 666, 288 450" style="--k:3"/><path d="M176 450 C 380 144, 822 212, 1128 450 S 924 722, 176 450" style="--k:4"/><path d="M64 450 C 310 81, 843 163, 1212 450 S 966 778, 64 450" style="--k:5"/><path d="M-48 450 C 240 18, 864 114, 1296 450 S 1008 834, -48 450" style="--k:6"/><path d="M-160 450 C 170 -45, 885 65, 1380 450 S 1050 890, -160 450" style="--k:7"/><path d="M-272 450 C 100 -108, 906 16, 1464 450 S 1092 946, -272 450" style="--k:8"/></svg><div class="wm-w wm-hero-g"><div class="wm-hero-t"><p class="wm-ey"><i></i>Field notes on staying warm</p><h1><span>Warm</span><span>ers</span></h1><p class="wm-hero-p">An independent guide to warm jackets and layering, from city winters to frosty trails. What to wear, why it works and how to put it together.</p><div class="wm-hero-a"><a class="wm-btn" href="#layers">Build your layers</a><p class="wm-read"><b id="hero-t">-12</b>&deg;C<br><span>feels colder in the wind</span></p></div></div><div class="wm-hero-i"><div class="wm-frost pxw"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788088133486-d090adaa7db3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=760&h=960&q=75" alt="a woman in a fleece jacket outdoors" width="760" height="960" fetchpriority="high"></div><span class="wm-pin" aria-hidden="true">N 46&deg;32&prime; &middot; 2,140 m</span></div></div></section>

<div class="wm-mq mq" aria-hidden="true"><div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1557418669-db3f781a58c0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man wearing a warm jacket outdoors" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762224691220-96a3335008a6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man in a cap and fleece outdoors" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1770739982427-3169499c332e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person zipping up a dark jacket" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762224691127-56e7b1dce731?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man in a dark jacket in an autumn landscape" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788088133472-d0475dc876e4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="two people walking on a path in jackets" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768347441598-546c4b6d6512?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person in a warm jacket near the sea" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1557418669-db3f781a58c0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man wearing a warm jacket outdoors" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762224691220-96a3335008a6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man in a cap and fleece outdoors" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1770739982427-3169499c332e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person zipping up a dark jacket" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762224691127-56e7b1dce731?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a man in a dark jacket in an autumn landscape" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788088133472-d0475dc876e4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="two people walking on a path in jackets" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768347441598-546c4b6d6512?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person in a warm jacket near the sea" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div>

<section class="wm-s wm-in"><div class="wm-w wm-in-g"><p class="wm-big rv">Warmth is not about one thick coat. It is about <em>trapping still air</em>, blocking wind and letting sweat escape, in layers you can adjust.</p><div class="wm-in-n stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="3">3</b><span>layers: base, mid, outer</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="700">700</b><span>fill power: warm, light down</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="10">10</b><small>&deg;C</small><span>colder the wind can make it feel</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-s wm-ly" id="layers"><div class="wm-w wm-ly-g"><div><p class="wm-ey"><i></i>Layer builder</p><h2 class="rv">Stack your layers</h2><p class="wm-p">Switch layers on and off. Watch the rings build around the body and see how warm, dry and breathable you are.</p><div class="wm-tg" role="group" aria-label="Layers"><label><input type="checkbox" value="0" checked><span><b>Base</b>Merino or synthetic tee</span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="1" checked><span><b>Mid</b>Fleece or wool</span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="2"><span><b>Insulation</b>Down or synthetic jacket</span></label><label><input type="checkbox" value="3"><span><b>Shell</b>Waterproof, windproof</span></label></div></div><div class="wm-ly-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 360" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="180" cy="180" r="150" class="ring r3" id="ly3"/><circle cx="180" cy="180" r="122" class="ring r2" id="ly2"/><circle cx="180" cy="180" r="96" class="ring r1" id="ly1"/><circle cx="180" cy="180" r="72" class="ring r0" id="ly0"/><circle cx="180" cy="180" r="50" class="core"/><text x="180" y="186" text-anchor="middle" class="ct">you</text></svg><div class="wm-ly-o" id="ly-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-s wm-fill"><div class="wm-w"><div class="wm-fill-h"><p class="wm-ey"><i></i>Insulation</p><h2 class="rv">Four ways to stay warm</h2><p class="wm-p">Bars show warmth for weight, warmth when damp and breathability.</p></div><div class="wm-fls rv"><button type="button" class="wm-fl on" data-i="0" style="--c:#E2572B"><span>01</span><b>Down</b><em>Lightest for its warmth and packs tiny. Best in dry cold; loses warmth when soaked unless treated.</em><div class="wm-fl-b"><i style="width:100%"></i><i style="width:40%"></i><i style="width:90%"></i></div></button><button type="button" class="wm-fl" data-i="1" style="--c:#C99A3B"><span>02</span><b>Synthetic</b><em>Keeps warming when damp, dries fast and is easy to wash. A little heavier than down.</em><div class="wm-fl-b"><i style="width:80%"></i><i style="width:80%"></i><i style="width:60%"></i></div></button><button type="button" class="wm-fl" data-i="2" style="--c:#6E8B74"><span>03</span><b>Fleece</b><em>Breathable and comfortable on the move. Not windproof alone, so pair it with a shell.</em><div class="wm-fl-b"><i style="width:50%"></i><i style="width:90%"></i><i style="width:70%"></i></div></button><button type="button" class="wm-fl" data-i="3" style="--c:#8C7A66"><span>04</span><b>Wool</b><em>Warm when damp, resists odour and feels natural. Heavier, and slower to dry.</em><div class="wm-fl-b"><i style="width:70%"></i><i style="width:60%"></i><i style="width:50%"></i></div></button></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-s wm-tp" id="temp"><div class="wm-w wm-tp-g"><div class="wm-tp-th"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 420" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="40" y="20" width="40" height="320" rx="20" class="tb"/><rect x="48" y="40" width="24" height="300" rx="12" class="tt" id="tp-m"/><circle cx="60" cy="370" r="40" class="tbl"/><circle cx="60" cy="370" r="30" class="tm"/></svg><div class="wm-tp-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1776863037197-03ee58bcfbb4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=380&q=75" alt="a hiker in a red jacket on a mountain trail" width="520" height="380" loading="lazy"></div></div><div><p class="wm-ey"><i></i>Temperature guide</p><h2 class="rv">What should I wear today?</h2><label class="wm-lab" for="tp-s">Temperature <output id="tp-o">-5&deg;C</output><input type="range" id="tp-s" min="-25" max="15" value="-5"></label><div class="wm-act" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Activity"><label><input type="radio" name="ac" value="0" checked><span>Standing still</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ac" value="1"><span>Walking</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ac" value="2"><span>Hiking hard</span></label></div><div class="wm-tp-r" id="tp-r" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>

